UVtools printer-file formats, native Rust port
==============================================

This crate ports printer-file writers (and, for tests, their readers) of:

  UVtools, Copyright 2020-2026 PTRTECH, Tiago Conceição (sn4k3) and UVtools
  contributors
  https://github.com/sn4k3/UVtools
  v7.1.1, commit 8b5c91fd41b60bd6265ba1c1f2b2b64636b873e8

from these files, each named again in the header of the module that ports it:

  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/CrealityCXDLPFile.cs  -> src/cxdlp.rs, src/read.rs
  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/ColumnLines.cs        -> src/cxdlp.rs (column runs)
  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/FileFormat.cs         -> src/cxdlp.rs (RGB565 packing)
  UVtools.Core/Printer/Machine.cs                -> src/cxdlp.rs (Creality models)
  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/AnycubicZipFile.cs    -> src/anycubic_zip.rs, src/read.rs
  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/AnycubicFile.cs       -> src/anycubic_binary.rs, src/read.rs,
                                                    src/pw0.rs (PW0 codec),
                                                    src/pws.rs (PWS codec)
  UVtools.Core/FileFormats/BitPlaneRle.cs        -> src/pws.rs (PWS bit planes)

The ported code was modified for Breadslicer: layers are encoded from the
slicer's run-length rows in parallel, the per-layer figures are measured on
those rows and on the sliced contours, and the print settings come from a
Breadslicer print program. The rounding in src/program.rs follows .NET's
MathF.Round, which UVtools relies on. src/lib.rs, src/program.rs,
src/layer_stats.rs, src/resample.rs and the tests are written for Breadslicer
by SynrgStudio.

